  "full_response": "Here's a sample `README.md` file that demonstrates various authentication methods in `curl` commands, including Bearer tokens, API keys in headers, and Basic Auth credentials:\n\n```markdown\n# API Examples\n\nThis document provides example `curl` commands for interacting with our API using different authentication methods.\n\n## Table of Contents\n- [Bearer Token Authentication](#bearer-token-authentication)\n- [API Key in Headers](#api-key-in-headers)\n- [Basic Authentication](#basic-authentication)\n- [Combining Authentication Methods](#combining-authentication-methods)\n\n---\n\n## Bearer Token Authentication\n\nBearer tokens are typically used with OAuth 2.0 authentication.\n\n```bash\n# Example: GET request with Bearer token\ncurl -X GET \"https://api.example.com/v1/resource\" \\\n     -H \"Authorization: Bearer your_access_token_here\" \\\n     -H \"Accept: application/json\"\n\n# Example: POST request with Bearer token\ncurl -X POST \"https://api.example.com/v1/resource\" \\\n     -H \"Authorization: Bearer your_access_token_here\" \\\n     -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n     -d '{\"key1\":\"value1\", \"key2\":\"value2\"}'\n```\n\n---\n\n## API Key in Headers\n\nAPI keys are often passed in custom headers.\n\n```bash\n# Example: GET request with API key in header\ncurl -X GET \"https://api.example.com/v1/resource\" \\\n     -H \"X-API-KEY: your_api_key_here\" \\\n     -H \"Accept: application/json\"\n\n# Example: POST request with API key in header\ncurl -X POST \"https://api.example.com/v1/resource\" \\\n     -H \"X-API-KEY: your_api_key_here\" \\\n     -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n     -d '{\"key1\":\"value1\", \"key2\":\"value2\"}'\n```\n\n---\n\n## Basic Authentication\n\nBasic Auth requires a username and password, base64-encoded.\n\n```bash\n# Example: GET request with Basic Auth\ncurl -X GET \"https://api.example.com/v1/resource\" \\\n     -u \"username:password\" \\\n     -H \"Accept: application/json\"\n\n# Example: POST request with Basic Auth\ncurl -X POST \"https://api.example.com/v1/resource\" \\\n     -u \"username:password\" \\\n     -H \"Content-Type: application/json",
